From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: reset the decode engine on a codec switch

VP9 runs on the H.265 engine and leaves registers set that H.265 never
writes. With VP9 and H.265 decoding at once on the H713, every H.265 job
fails its slice-header setup ("Failed to setup decoding job: -22") while
VP9 stays bit-exact; GStreamer hands out stale buffers with exit status
0. Each codec alone, and two H.265 streams at once, are bit-exact.
Sequential streams are unaffected because runtime PM resets the engine
between them. Reproduced 4/4 on the H713 bench.

well0nez found this and resets the engine with RST_BUS_VE whenever a job's
codec differs from the last one's (their 0298). On the H713 that line
also gates the AV1 core's bus. They measured that a pulse into an AV1
frame in flight stalls the core and then the SoC, which led to a reset
guard (0305-0307).

The H713 decode engine has its own reset, RST_BUS_VE3, which the AV1 core
does not use. Pulse only that line, and only where the VE3 reset exists,
before a job's first register write; m2m runs one job at a time, so the
engine is idle. A failed pulse leaves the codec unrecorded so the next job
retries. Runtime resume clears the record, since the engine leaves reset
clean.

Measured with a diagnostic build:

- With no reset, H.265 fails in 4/4 VP9+H.265 pairs.
- A VE3-only pulse and a full VE pulse both make all pairs bit-exact
  (about 1000 pulses each, no measurable cost).
- With AV1 bound, AV1 decoded 40/40 clips bit-exact (720p and 1080p) beside
  138 s of VP9+H.265 switching and 5064 VE3 pulses. Cedrus stayed 40/40
  exact, with no AV1 errors or timeouts.

So the codec-switch reset needs no AV1 arbitration.

Link: https://github.com/well0nez/allwinner-h713-linux/blob/149f51d0df24c45b12674c81aab128b1fc8f5d4b/mainline/patches/kernel/0298-media-cedrus-a-job-of-another-codec-starts-from-a-reset-engine.patch

---

--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.h
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.h
@@ -268,6 +268,8 @@
 
 	struct reset_control	*rstc;
 	struct reset_control	*rstc_ve3;
+	/* codec of the last job, to reset the decode engine on a switch */
+	u32			last_codec;
 
 	unsigned int		capabilities;
 
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_dec.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_dec.c
@@ -30,6 +30,8 @@
 	struct media_request *src_req;
 	int error;
 
+	cedrus_reset_on_codec_switch(dev, ctx->src_fmt.pixelformat);
+
 	run.src = v4l2_m2m_next_src_buf(ctx->fh.m2m_ctx);
 	run.dst = v4l2_m2m_next_dst_buf(ctx->fh.m2m_ctx);
 
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_hw.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_hw.c
@@ -474,6 +474,47 @@
 					 VB2_BUF_STATE_ERROR);
 }
 
+/*
+ * A job of another codec than the last one starts from a reset decode
+ * engine. VP9 runs on the H.265 engine and leaves registers set that H.265
+ * never writes, such as its frame header at +0x504: with VP9 and H.265
+ * decoding at once, every H.265 job failed its slice-header setup
+ * (-EINVAL) while VP9 stayed bit-exact (found by well0nez, their 0298).
+ * Sequential streams are unaffected, because runtime PM resets the engine
+ * between them. Every codec programs the engine in full for each job.
+ *
+ * Their fix pulses RST_BUS_VE. On the H713 that line also gates the AV1
+ * core's bus; well0nez measured that a pulse into an AV1 frame in flight
+ * stalls the core and then the SoC. The decode engine has its own reset,
+ * RST_BUS_VE3, which
+ * the AV1 core does not use: pulsing it clears the residue (VP9+H.265
+ * pairs bit-exact), and AV1 decoded bit-exact beside thousands of such
+ * pulses. So only VE3 is pulsed, and only where it exists.
+ *
+ * Called before a job's first register write; m2m runs one job at a time,
+ * so the engine is idle. A failed pulse leaves the codec unrecorded so the
+ * next job tries again.
+ */
+void cedrus_reset_on_codec_switch(struct cedrus_dev *dev, u32 codec)
+{
+	int ret;
+
+	if (!dev->rstc_ve3)
+		return;
+
+	if (dev->last_codec && dev->last_codec != codec) {
+		ret = reset_control_reset(dev->rstc_ve3);
+		if (ret) {
+			dev_warn_ratelimited(dev->dev,
+					     "decode engine reset on codec switch failed: %d\n",
+					     ret);
+			return;
+		}
+	}
+
+	dev->last_codec = codec;
+}
+
 int cedrus_hw_suspend(struct device *device)
 {
 	struct cedrus_dev *dev = dev_get_drvdata(device);
@@ -513,6 +554,8 @@
 			goto err_rst;
 		}
 	}
+	/* The engine leaves reset clean; no codec state to clear yet. */
+	dev->last_codec = 0;
 
 	ret = clk_prepare_enable(dev->ahb_clk);
 	if (ret) {
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_hw.h
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_hw.h
@@ -30,5 +30,6 @@
 void cedrus_hw_remove(struct cedrus_dev *dev);
 
 void cedrus_watchdog(struct work_struct *work);
+void cedrus_reset_on_codec_switch(struct cedrus_dev *dev, u32 codec);
 
 #endif
